    "type": "WSI",
    "diagnosis": "<p>Gastric adenocarcinoma metastatic to the breast:&nbsp;</p>",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>Core biopsies show malignant cells invading the breast stroma, in between and into breast lobules.&nbsp; The malignant cells have&nbsp;hyperchromatic nuclei that are sometimes eccentric, giving a signet ring-like appearance.&nbsp; Mitoses and cytoplasmic vacuoles are present.&nbsp; There was a past history of gastric adenocarcinoma, and immunohistochemical studies&nbsp;supported metastasis of gastric origin.</p>",
