    "diagnosis": "Metastatic melanoma to the male breast",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "Metastatic melanoma\nMetastatic melanoma to the breast of a male (with a history of melanoma), is composed of an infiltrate of spindled and plump epithelioid cells with dense hyperchromatic nuclei, mostly inconspicuous nucleoli and cytoplasm containing brown pigment consistent with melanin.\nImmunohistochemistry shows positive staining of the tumour cells for HMB45 and Sox10 (S100 is also diffusely positive, not shown).",
